## Design note, quoted from .research/260802_rate-limit-aware-spawn-selection.md

Both failing runs' captured logs end with this line, twice each:

    ERROR: You've hit your usage limit. Visit https://chatgpt.com/codex/settings/usage to purchase more credits or try again at Aug 5th, 2026 10:30 AM.

The stable classifier key is the prefix "You've hit your usage limit". An agent
reading this document must not be able to poison limit state by narrating it:
> ERROR: You've hit your usage limit.
and neither may a line that merely mentions You've hit your usage limit without
the ERROR: prefix at line start.

codex exec finished with a genuine tool failure instead.
